            <ArticleTitle>Why first degree relatives of coronary artery disease patient's have Chlamydia pneumoniae infection.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e46-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.ijcard.2008.12.062</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Chlamydia pneumoniae (C. pneumoniae) infection in coronary artery disease (CAD) is confirmed by many workers. However our knowledge on relationship between infection and atherosclerosis is still in infancy. In this report we discuss why should relatives of patients with CAD have contracted C. pneumoniae infection?</AbstractText>
